.*****************************************************************
.*  Provide all the help for the command together in one help ID
.*  so that it can be used by a search index.
.*****************************************************************
:HELP name='CHGOBJDA/ALL'.
:IMHELP name=CHGOBJDA.
:IMHELP name='CHGOBJDA/OBJ'.
:IMHELP name='CHGOBJDA/OBJTYPE'.
:IMHELP name='CHGOBJDA/SRCF'.
:IMHELP name='CHGOBJDA/SRCFLIB'.
:IMHELP name='CHGOBJDA/SRCMBR'.
:IMHELP name='CHGOBJDA/SRCDATE'.
:IMHELP name='CHGOBJDA/SRCTIME'.
:IMHELP name='CHGOBJDA/OBJLVL'.
:IMHELP name='CHGOBJDA/LICPGM'.
:IMHELP name='CHGOBJDA/PTF'.
:IMHELP name='CHGOBJDA/APAR'.
:IMHELP name='CHGOBJDA/USRDFNATR'.
:EHELP.

.*****************************************************************
.*  Primary help text for the command.
.*****************************************************************
:HELP NAME='CHGOBJDA'.
Change Object Description Attr - Help
:P.
The Change Object Description Attr (CHGOBJDA) command changes
various attributes of an object description.
:P.
Although the command originally was designed to help us to
customize a change management product CHGOBJDA can also be used
stand alone.
:EHELP.

.*****************************************************************
.*  Help text for the command parameters.
.*****************************************************************

.********************************************
.*  Keyword:  OBJ
.********************************************
:HELP NAME='CHGOBJDA/OBJ'.
Object (OBJ) - Help

:XH3.Object (OBJ)

:P.
Specifies the qualified name of the object whose attributes
are being changed.  If no library name is given, *LIBL
is used to find the specified object. The library name
is entered to ensure that the correct object is being
specified.

:IMHELP name='COM/REQPARM'.
:P.
The possible :HP2.Object name:EHP2. values are:

:PARML.
:PT.:PV.Object name:EPV.
:PD.Specify the name of the object to be changed.
:EPARML.
:P.

The possible library values are:

:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*LIBL:EPK.
:PD.All libraries in the job's library list are searched
until the first match is found.
:PT.:PV.*CURLIB:EPV.
:PD.The current library for the job is used to locate the
object. If no library is specified as the current
library for the job, QGPL is used.
:PT.:PV.Library name:EPV.
:PD.Specify the name of the libary.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.

.********************************************
.*  Keyword:  OBJTYPE
.********************************************
:HELP NAME='CHGOBJDA/OBJTYPE'.
Object type (OBJTYPE) - Help

:XH3.Object type (OBJTYPE)

:P.
Specifies the object type of the object that is being changed.  For a
complete list of object types, position the cursor on the field for the
:HP2.Object type:EHP2. prompt (OBJTYPE parameter), and press F4.

:IMHELP name='COM/REQPARM'.
:P.
:IMHELP name='COM/VALUES'.

:PARML.
:PT.:PV.object-type:EPV.
:PD.Specify the predefined value that identifies the
object type to be changed.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.

.********************************************
.*  Keyword:  SRCF
.********************************************
:HELP NAME='CHGOBJDA/SRCF'.
Source file (SRCF) - Help

:XH3.Source file (SRCF)

:P.
Specifies the name of the source file that contains the
source member that was used to create the object.

:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
:P.
:IMHELP name='COM/VALUES'.

:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The source file name does not change.
:PT.:PV.*BLANK:EPV.
:PD.The source file name is not specified.
:PT.:PV.source-file-name:EPV.
:PD.Enter the name of the source file that contains the
source member that was used to create the object.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.

.********************************************
.*  Keyword:  SRCFLIB
.********************************************
:HELP NAME='CHGOBJDA/SRCFLIB'.
Source file library (SRCFLIB) - Help

:XH3.Source file library (SRCFLIB)

:P.
Specifies the name of the library that contains the source file
that contains the source member that was used to create the object.

:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
:P.
:IMHELP name='COM/VALUES'.

:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The name of the library does not change.
:PT.:PV.*BLANK:EPV.
:PD.The name of the library is not specified.
:PT.:PV.library-name:EPV.
:PD.Specifies the name of the library that contains the source file
that contains the source member that was used to create the object.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.

.********************************************
.*  Keyword:  SRCMBR
.********************************************
:HELP NAME='CHGOBJDA/SRCMBR'.
Source member (SRCMBR) - Help

:XH3.Source member (SRCMBR)

:P.
Specifies the name of the member of the source file that
contains the source that was used to create the object.

:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
:P.
:IMHELP name='COM/VALUES'.

:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The name of the member of the source file does not change.
:PT.:PV.*BLANK:EPV.
:PD.The name of the member of the source file is not specified.
:PT.:PV.source-file-member-name:EPV.
:PD.Specifies the name of the member of the source file that
contains the source that was used to create the object.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.

.********************************************
.*  Keyword:  SRCDATE
.********************************************
:HELP NAME='CHGOBJDA/SRCDATE'.
Source member change date (SRCDATE) - Help

:XH3.Source member change date (SRCDATE)

:P.
In a source physical file, the change date is the date
that the content of the file was last changed.

:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
:P.
:IMHELP name='COM/VALUES'.

:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The change date does not change.
:PT.:PV.*SRCMBR:EPV.
:PD.The change date is set to the change date retrieved from the
source member specified at the :HP2.Source member:EHP2. (SRCMBR) parameter.
:PT.:PV.Last-change-date:EPV.
:PD.Date that the content of the file was last changed.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.

.********************************************
.*  Keyword:  SRCTIME
.********************************************
:HELP NAME='CHGOBJDA/SRCTIME'.
Source member change date (SRCTIME) - Help

:XH3.Source member change time (SRCTIME)

:P.
In a source physical file, the change time is the time
that the content of the file was last changed.

:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
:P.
:IMHELP name='COM/VALUES'.

:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The change time does not change.
:PT.:PV.*SRCMBR:EPV.
:PD.The change time is set to the change time retrieved from the
source member specified at the :HP2.Source member:EHP2. (SRCMBR) parameter.
:PT.:PV.Last-change-date:EPV.
:PD.Time that the content of the file was last changed.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.

.********************************************
.*  Keyword:  OBJLVL
.********************************************
:HELP NAME='CHGOBJDA/OBJLVL'.
Object Control Level (OBJLVL) - Help

:XH3.Object Control Level (OBJLVL)

:P.
The object control level of the object should be a unique
identifier that is changed with every changes applied to the object.
:P.
The object control level is used by the change management software
to store the task number that the object was assigned to.
:P.
:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
:P.
:IMHELP name='COM/VALUES'.

:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The object control level does not change.
:PT.:PV.*BLANK:EPV.
:PD.The object control level is not specified.
:PT.:PV.The object control level:EPV.
:PD.Specify the object control level of the object.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.

.********************************************
.*  Keyword:  LICPGM
.********************************************
:HELP NAME='CHGOBJDA/LICPGM'.
Licensed program (LICPGM) - Help

:XH3.Licensed program (LICPGM)

:P.
If the object is part of a licensed program, then this
field shows the product number and the level of the
licensed program.
:P.
:LINES.
Position  1- 7:  Licensed program identifier
Position  8- 9:  Version
Position 10-11:  Release
Position 12-13:  Modification level
:ELINES.
:P.
The licensed program is used by the change management software
to store the modification level of the object.
:P.
:LINES.
Position  1- 3:  Version (*MAJOR)
Position     4:  Point   (.)
Position  5- 7:  Version (*MINOR)
Position  8- 9:  Release
Position    10:  Point   (.)
Position 11-12:  Level
Position    13:  not used
:ELINES.
:P.
:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
:P.
:IMHELP name='COM/VALUES'.

:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The licensed program does not change.
:PT.:PV.*BLANK:EPV.
:PD.The licensed program is not specified.
:PT.:PV.Licensed-program:EPV.
:PD.Specify the license program that the object is part of.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.

.********************************************
.*  Keyword:  PTF
.********************************************
:HELP NAME='CHGOBJDA/PTF'.
PTF number (PTF) - Help

:XH3.PTF number (PTF)

:P.
The Program Temporary Fix that resulted in the creation of
the displayed object.
:P.
The PTF number is used by the change management software
to store the form number that moved the object.
:P.

:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
:P.
:IMHELP name='COM/VALUES'.

:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The PTF number does not change.
:PT.:PV.*BLANK:EPV.
:PD.The PTF number is not specified.
:PT.:PV.PTF number:EPV.
:PD.The Program Temporary Fix that resulted in the creation of
the displayed object.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.

.********************************************
.*  Keyword:  APAR
.********************************************
:HELP NAME='CHGOBJDA/APAR'.
APAR ID (APAR) - Help

:XH3.APAR ID (APAR)

:P.
The displayed object has been patched as the result of the
Authorized Program Analysis Report (APAR) with this
identification number.
:P.
The APAR ID is used by the change management software
to store the application ID the object is part of.
:P.
:LINES.
Position  1- 4:  Application
Position  5- 6:  unknown
:ELINES.
:P.

:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
:P.
:IMHELP name='COM/VALUES'.

:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The APAR ID does not change.
:PT.:PV.*BLANK:EPV.
:PD.The APAR ID is not specified.
:PT.:PV.APAR-ID:EPV.
:PD.The APAR ID that resulted in the creation of
the displayed object.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.

.********************************************
.*  Keyword:  USRDFNATR
.********************************************
:HELP NAME='CHGOBJDA/USRDFNATR'.
Benutzerdefiniertes Attribut (USRDFNATR) - Help

:XH3.User-defined attribute (USRDFNATR)

:P.
The user-defined attribute can be used to identifies
an object type further.
:P.
The user-defined attribute is used by the change management software
to store the type code the object is part of.
:P.

:IMHELP name='COM/OPTPARM'.
:P.
:IMHELP name='COM/VALUES'.

:PARML.
:PT.:PK DEF.*SAME:EPK.
:PD.The user-defined attribute does not change
:PT.:PV.*BLANK:EPV.
:PD.The user-defined attribute is not specified.
:PT.:PV.User-defined attribute :EPV.
:PD.The user-defined attribute that specifies the object further.
:EPARML.
:EHELP.

